{"Large, invasive change to the caching layer of identity providers spanning create(), update(), remove(), and a new getForLogin cache path is a common source of subtle correctness bugs (stale data shown on login pages, over/under-invalidation, race conditions)": 0.09372173994779587, "The new getForLogin implementation introduces multiple code paths (query==null vs existing query vs cached entry missing) with added cache operations using different revision strategies (cache.addRevisioned(cacheKey, startupRevision) vs cache.addRevisioned(..., cache.getCurrentCounter())) which increases complexity and potential for bugs": 0.09776034951210022}